    "findings": [],
    "checked_invariants": [
      {
        "area": "Repeated-name work",
        "evidence": "dtd.rs::attlist_attribute charges element.len() after the first committed attribute before both Captured(None) and Silent returns. This preserves ordinary repeated-name work independently of handler presence. Default definitions, attribute count limits, default-value expansion and selected allocator fallibility remain before callback suppression. The older Enumeration(None) branch belongs to the unchanged external grammar path and is not used by the new ordinary continuation."
      },
      {
        "area": "Bounded progressive work",
        "evidence": "attlist.rs advances a lexical fragment boundary, advances the grammar cursor, or returns a queued event; the empty suffix is handled before fragment_length. Enumeration members are consumed before their metadata yield. PositionCursor scans only the delta since its last offset; raw counts cover the current fragment, so it does not repeatedly scan a complete prior token prefix. Attribute semantic parsing rescans only its own commit span. Captured enumeration storage is one attribute at a time and uses the selected allocator."
      },
      {
        "area": "Continuation and shared tables",
        "evidence": "The complete lexical Buffer, element name, cursor and captured enum string are owned in the boxed state. The owner is restored before successful callback yields and drops on errors. No table entry or input slice survives a core operation. parse_dtd_step resumes the state before inspecting or consuming source input; the source remains unconsumed until final closure. Appended feeds retain offsets; source compaction occurs on consume. The ordinary input context therefore retains the declaration anchor. Shared DTD scope ends before returning owned events to the C adapter."
      },
      {
        "area": "Source and alias provenance",
        "evidence": "The initial scanner accounts and bounds the complete token before creating the continuation. Grammar consumes the lexical view, while element/type/default/raw payloads decode only their original Slice spans. PositionCursor retains raw-width, CR/LF and anchored entity semantics. Error offsets still use the unchanged source view; the token is consumed once after the closing delimiter."
      },
      {
        "area": "Callback mutation and reentry",
        "evidence": "Default and ATTLIST availability are read at each semantic/fragment boundary. Member capture is separate from the full stored attribute type; absent members suppress only the callback. Event payloads and C strings are owned before callback invocation. attlist_dispatch is set after all fallible CString conversions and cleared after the synchronous callback, and starts false for creation/reset/children. XML_DefaultCurrent creates an allocation-free empty String only during that ATTLIST dispatch; existing busy/default-recursion and allocator-reentry guards remain. The single-fragment Default optimization preserves the same owned queue/drain path and bypasses duplicate filtering only when duplicate_default is absent."
      },
      {
        "area": "No unsafe simplification recommended",
        "evidence": "The apparent repeated grammar parse serves distinct lexical callback boundaries versus semantic definition construction. Combining it or treating Silent and Captured(None) as interchangeable would alter member-capture, position or Default behavior. No larger rewrite is needed to accept this bounded patch."
      }
    ],
    "test_source_observations": [
      "Inspected the exact-work boundary matrix including handler installation/removal and captured-none enums; it asserts both final outcome and expansion counter.",
      "Inspected owned-token feed/compaction, child publication, malformed later attributes and bounded pending-queue regressions.",
      "Inspected selected-allocation workload additions and C lifecycle tests for handler installation, DefaultCurrent, suspension, reset/free rejection during callbacks, and UTF16/chunk variants."
    ],
    "limits": [
      "This is a source review, not an independent rerun of the author 365 tests, 4740 upstream cases or existing 3656-record oracle.",
      "The complete declaration token is still buffered and lexically validated before its first attribute callback; partial-token timing and malformed-prefix callback parity are not newly claimed.",
